body:
Please notice that a similar bug also happens with line breaks inside the rule description. The following valid output of a minifier:

.push{margin:5px
-160px 1.5em 160px}

 is converted into

.push {
  margin: -155px 1.5em 160px;
}

The maths are computed between the first two items, and I get a subtraction!

@default007: This is a different thing. 

File a new bug.

It's actually the intended behavior but I agree with you that is not what should happen. It would be better if a math expression has to  be inside @(...) or something in order to avoid these kind of problems. Right now the way to go around this is using escaping ~"..."
 In your example:
.push{margin: ~"5px -160px 1.5em 160px"}

I think it would be better to specify (because less common) when an arithmetic operation is expected instead of having to specify when it is not expected.

